Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/cofflink.c
Line: 1670
Function: coff_renumber_symbols
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: For a tag symbol with n_numaux == 1, bfd_coff_swap_aux_in reads the aux entry at esym + isymesz without verifying that the symbol table actually contains that aux (i.e., esym + isymesz <= esym_end). A truncated or malformed symbol table can cause an OOB read.

